-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg9, LAYER 1: Subchapter XII, sections 311 to 314.
-- Revocation of voluntary dissolution; restoration of an expired certificate of incorporation; revival of a
-- forfeited or void certificate; revival for exempt corporations; status of a corporation that renews, extends
-- and continues its existence.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550). It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is
-- line N of that file (an ellipsis means the line goes on).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view: each rule is the relation the text states between the corporation, its
-- directors, officers and stockholders, the Secretary of State and the State. The Court of Chancery's discretion
-- is a plain input and is never guessed.
--
-- Sections 311, 312 and 313 are listed in section 114(b)(1): the section 114(a) reading (stockholder as member) does
-- not touch them, and each states its own rule for a nonstock corporation (subsections 311(f), 312(j), 313).
-- This module imports dg9-x-winding-up.l4 for the one rule both modules need: the period of section 278.
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: sections 103, 131(c), 136(b), 204, 211(c), 222, 228, 284 and 371 (pieces dg1 to dg5,
-- dg10 and dg11 as the NOTES.md table says), and chapter 5 of the Law (franchise taxes; sections 501, 502 and 510), which
-- is not among the inputs. The range holds no commencement rule and no date of enactment (NOTES.md).

§ `Subchapter XII. Renewal, Revival, Extension and Restoration of Certificate of Incorporation or Charter`

§§ `s 311 Revocation of voluntary dissolution; restoration of expired certificate of incorporation`

-- "At any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the dissolution of a corporation pursuant to § 275 of this
-- title or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, or at any
-- time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the expiration of the time limited for the corporation’s existence
-- ... or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278": this is the period of section
-- 278, so section 278's rule is used and not written again. The step that must fall in the period is the filing of the
-- certificate of revocation or restoration; the last day of the period is inside it (fork F12).
-- src:1584 | At any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the dissolution of a corporation pursuant to § 275 of this title or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(a) (src:1584)
GIVEN `the date the dissolution became effective, or the time limited for the corporation’s existence expired` IS A DATE
      `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued under section 278, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the certificate of revocation of dissolution or of restoration is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 311(a) the revocation of the dissolution or the restoration is within the time allowed` MEANS
    `the date the certificate of revocation of dissolution or of restoration is filed` AT MOST (`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS `the date the dissolution became effective, or the time limited for the corporation’s existence expired`, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued under section 278, if it has`)

-- (a)(1): "For purposes of this section, the term “stockholders” shall mean the stockholders of record on the date the
-- dissolution became effective or the date of expiration by limitation." (a)(3): notice of the special meeting is given
-- to each of the stockholders in accordance with section 222.
-- src:1585 | (1) For purposes of this section, the term “stockholders” shall mean the stockholders of record on the date the dissolution became effective or the date of expiration by limitation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(a)(1) (src:1585)
GIVEN `the person was a stockholder of record on the date the dissolution became effective or on the date of expiration by limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 311(a)(1) the person is one of the stockholders for the purposes of section 311` MEANS
    `the person was a stockholder of record on the date the dissolution became effective or on the date of expiration by limitation`

-- (a)(2) to (a)(4): the board adopts a resolution recommending the revocation or restoration and directing that the
-- question be put to a special meeting of stockholders; notice of the meeting is given to each of the stockholders in
-- accordance with section 222 (out of range: piece dg5); at the meeting "a majority of the stock of the corporation which
-- was outstanding and entitled to vote upon a dissolution at the time of its dissolution, in the case of a revocation of
-- dissolution, or which was outstanding and entitled to vote upon an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to
-- change the period of the corporation’s duration at the time of its expiration by limitation, in the case of a restoration,"
-- must vote for the resolution; or the stockholders give their written consent in accordance with section 228 (out of
-- range: piece dg5) "in lieu of a meeting and vote". The votes counted are those of the stock outstanding and entitled
-- to vote at that earlier time. The board's resolution is required on either route (fork F13).
-- src:1586 | (2) The board of directors shall adopt a resolution recommending that the dissolution be revoked in the case of a dissolution or that the certificate of incorporation be restored in the case of an expiration by limitation and directing that the question of the revocation or restoration be submitted to a vote at a special meeting of stockholders.
-- src:1587 | (3) Notice of the special meeting of stockholders shall be given in accordance with § 222 of this title to each of the stockholders.
-- src:1588 | At the meeting a vote of the stockholders shall be taken on a resolution to revoke the dissolution in the case of a dissolution or to restore the certificate of incorporation in the case of an expiration by limitation. If a majority of the stock of the corporation which was outstanding and entitled to vote upon a dissolution at the time of its dissolution, in the case of a revocation of dissolution, or which was outstanding and entitled to vote upon an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration at the time of its expiration by limitation, in the case of a restoration, shall be voted for the resolution, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(a)(2) to (a)(4) (src:1586-1588)
