@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(a)(4) (src:1588)
GIVEN `the event` IS A `s 311(a) Event ended by the certificate`
GIVETH A `Vote requirement`
`s 311(a)(4) the vote that revokes the dissolution or restores the certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `a dissolution pursuant to section 275` THEN `a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the stock of the corporation which was outstanding and entitled to vote upon a dissolution at the time of its dissolution")
    WHEN `an expiration of the time limited for the corporation’s existence` THEN `a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the stock of the corporation which was outstanding and entitled to vote upon an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration at the time of its expiration by limitation")

