GIVEN `the event` IS A `s 311(a) Event ended by the certificate`
      `the board of directors adopted a resolution recommending the revocation or restoration and directing that the question be submitted to a vote at a special meeting of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the special meeting was given to each of the stockholders in accordance with § 222` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 222 (piece dg5)
      `the votes voted for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes of the stock outstanding and entitled to vote at the time of the dissolution or the expiration` IS A NUMBER
      `the stockholders have given their written consent in lieu of a meeting and vote, in accordance with § 228` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 228 (piece dg5)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311(a) the revocation of the dissolution or the restoration of the certificate is authorized` MEANS
    IF NOT `the board of directors adopted a resolution recommending the revocation or restoration and directing that the question be submitted to a vote at a special meeting of stockholders`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the stockholders have given their written consent in lieu of a meeting and vote, in accordance with § 228`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`s 311(a)(4) the vote that revokes the dissolution or restores the certificate` `the event`) `the votes voted for the resolution` `the votes of the stock outstanding and entitled to vote at the time of the dissolution or the expiration`
              WHEN JUST carried THEN JUST (carried AND `notice of the special meeting was given to each of the stockholders in accordance with § 222`)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (a)(4)a. to h.: the certificate, "specifically designated as a certificate of revocation of dissolution or a certificate of
-- restoration in its heading", states the name; the registered office and agent; the names and addresses of the officers
-- and the directors; the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation; the date of filing of the certificate
-- of dissolution; the vote or the written consent; and, "in the case of a restoration, the new specified date limiting
-- the duration of the corporation’s existence or that the corporation shall have perpetual existence".
