-- Subsection (f): a nonstock corporation may revoke its dissolution or restore its certificate within the same period "in a
-- manner analogous to that by which the dissolution was authorized or, in the case of a restoration, in the manner in
-- which an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration would have
-- been authorized": the manner is the nonstock corporation's own and needs a certificate "containing information
-- comparable to that required by paragraph (a)(4)". "Notwithstanding the foregoing, only subsections (b), (d), and (e)
-- of this section shall apply to nonstock corporations." Which subsections apply to which kind is a rule of its own.
-- src:1601 | (f) At any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the dissolution of a nonstock corporation pursuant to § 276 of this title or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, or at any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the expiration of the time limited for a nonstock corporation’s existence as provided in its certificate of incorporation or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, a nonstock corporation may revoke the dissolution theretofore effected by it or restore its certificate of incorporation after it has expired by limitation in a manner analogous to that by which the dissolution was authorized or, in the case of a restoration, in the manner in which an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration would have been authorized at the time of its expiration by limitation including (i) if applicable, a vote of the members entitled to vote, if any, on the dissolution or the amendment and (ii) the filing of a certificate of revocation of dissolution or a certificate of restoration containing information comparable to that required by paragraph (a)(4) of this section. Notwithstanding the foregoing, only subsections (b), (d), and (e) of this section shall apply to nonstock corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(f) (src:1601)
DECLARE `s 311 Subsection of section 311` IS ONE OF
    `subsection (a) of section 311`
    `subsection (b) of section 311`
    `subsection (c) of section 311`
    `subsection (d) of section 311`
    `subsection (e) of section 311`
    `subsection (f) of section 311`
    `subsection (g) of section 311`

-- src:1601 | (f) At any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the dissolution of a nonstock corporation pursuant to § 276 of this title or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, or at any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the expiration of the time limited for a nonstock corporation’s existence as provided in its certificate of incorporation or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, a nonstock corporation may revoke the dissolution theretofore effected by it or restore its certificate of incorporation after it has expired by limitation in a manner analogous to that by which the dissolution was authorized or, in the case of a restoration, in the manner in which an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration would have been authorized at the time of its expiration by limitation including (i) if applicable, a vote of the members entitled to vote, if any, on the dissolution or the amendment and (ii) the filing of a certificate of revocation of dissolution or a certificate of restoration containing information comparable to that required by paragraph (a)(4) of this section. Notwithstanding the foregoing, only subsections (b), (d), and (e) of this section shall apply to nonstock corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(f) (src:1601)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the subsection` IS A `s 311 Subsection of section 311`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 311(f) the subsection of section 311 applies to the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the subsection`
          WHEN `subsection (b) of section 311` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `subsection (d) of section 311` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `subsection (e) of section 311` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `subsection (f) of section 311` THEN TRUE
          OTHERWISE FALSE)
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the subsection`
          WHEN `subsection (f) of section 311` THEN FALSE
          OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- src:1601 | (f) At any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the dissolution of a nonstock corporation pursuant to § 276 of this title or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, or at any time prior to the expiration of 3 years following the expiration of the time limited for a nonstock corporation’s existence as provided in its certificate of incorporation or such longer period as the Court of Chancery may have directed pursuant to § 278 of this title, a nonstock corporation may revoke the dissolution theretofore effected by it or restore its certificate of incorporation after it has expired by limitation in a manner analogous to that by which the dissolution was authorized or, in the case of a restoration, in the manner in which an amendment to the certificate of incorporation to change the period of the corporation’s duration would have been authorized at the time of its expiration by limitation including (i) if applicable, a vote of the members entitled to vote, if any, on the dissolution or the amendment and (ii) the filing of a certificate of revocation of dissolution or a certificate of restoration containing information comparable to that required by paragraph (a)(4) of this section. Notwithstanding the foregoing, only subsections (b), (d), and (e) of this section shall apply to nonstock corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(f) (src:1601)
GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `s 311(a)(4) Certificate of revocation of dissolution or of restoration`
      `the event` IS A `s 311(a) Event ended by the certificate`
      `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vote of the members entitled to vote, if any, on the dissolution or the amendment was taken, if applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 311(f) the nonstock corporation’s revocation or restoration is authorized and certified as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `a vote of the members entitled to vote, if any, on the dissolution or the amendment was taken, if applicable`
    AND `s 311(a)(4) the certificate of revocation of dissolution or of restoration is in order` WITH `the certificate` IS `the certificate`, `the event` IS `the event`, `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`

-- Subsection (g): "Any corporation that revokes its dissolution or restores its certificate of incorporation pursuant to this
-- section shall file all annual franchise tax reports that the corporation would have had to file if it had not dissolved or
-- expired and shall pay all franchise taxes that the corporation would have had to pay if it had not dissolved or expired.
-- No payment made pursuant to this subsection shall reduce the amount of franchise tax due under Chapter 5 of this
-- title for the year in which such revocation or restoration is effected." Chapter 5 is not among the inputs: the figures
-- are plain inputs.
-- src:1602 | (g) Any corporation that revokes its dissolution or restores its certificate of incorporation pursuant to this section shall file all annual franchise tax reports that the corporation would have had to file if it had not dissolved or expired and shall pay all franchise taxes that the corporation would have had to pay if it had not dissolved or expired. No payment made pursuant to this subsection shall reduce the amount of franchise tax due under Chapter 5 of this title for the year in which such revocation or restoration is effected.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(g) (src:1602)
GIVEN `the franchise taxes the corporation would have had to pay if it had not dissolved or expired` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: chapter 5 of the Law is not among the inputs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 311(g) the franchise taxes the corporation must pay on revoking its dissolution or restoring its certificate` MEANS
    `the franchise taxes the corporation would have had to pay if it had not dissolved or expired`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 311(g) (src:1602)
GIVEN `the franchise tax due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revocation or restoration is effected` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: chapter 5 of the Law is not among the inputs
      `the payment made pursuant to subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 311(g) the franchise tax still due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revocation or restoration is effected` MEANS
    `the franchise tax due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revocation or restoration is effected`

§§ `s 312 Revival of certificate of incorporation`

-- Subsection (a): "As used in this section, the term “certificate of incorporation” includes the charter of a corporation
-- organized under any special act or any law of this State."
-- src:1606 | (a) As used in this section, the term “certificate of incorporation” includes the charter of a corporation organized under any special act or any law of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(a) (src:1606)
GIVEN `the instrument is a certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is the charter of a corporation organized under any special act or any law of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(a) the instrument is a certificate of incorporation for the purposes of section 312` MEANS
    `the instrument is a certificate of incorporation` OR `the instrument is the charter of a corporation organized under any special act or any law of this State`

-- Subsection (b): "Any corporation whose certificate of incorporation has become forfeited or void pursuant to this title may
-- at any time procure a revival of its certificate of incorporation ... by complying with the requirements of this section.
-- Notwithstanding the foregoing, this section shall not be applicable to a corporation whose certificate of incorporation
-- has been revoked or forfeited pursuant to § 284 of this title."
-- src:1607 | (b) Any corporation whose certificate of incorporation has become forfeited or void pursuant to this title may at any time procure a revival of its certificate of incorporation, together with all the rights, franchises, privileges and immunities and subject to all of its duties, debts and liabilities which had been secured or imposed by its original certificate of incorporation and all amendments thereto, by complying with the requirements of this section. Notwithstanding the foregoing, this section shall not be applicable to a corporation whose certificate of incorporation has been revoked or forfeited pursuant to § 284 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(b) (src:1607)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation has become forfeited or void pursuant to this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation has been revoked or forfeited pursuant to § 284` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(b) the corporation may procure a revival of its certificate of incorporation` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation has become forfeited or void pursuant to this title`
    AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation has been revoked or forfeited pursuant to § 284`)

-- Subsection (c): the revival "may be procured as authorized by the board of directors or members of the governing body of
-- the corporation in accordance with subsection (h) of this section and by executing, acknowledging and filing a certificate
-- of revival in accordance with § 103 of this title."
-- src:1608 | (c) The revival of the certificate of incorporation may be procured as authorized by the board of directors or members of the governing body of the corporation in accordance with subsection (h) of this section and by executing, acknowledging and filing a certificate of revival in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(c) (src:1608)
GIVEN `the board of directors or members of the governing body authorized the revival in accordance with subsection (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of revival was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(c) the revival is procured` MEANS
        `the board of directors or members of the governing body authorized the revival in accordance with subsection (h)`
    AND `the certificate of revival was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`

-- Subsection (d): the certificate states (1) the date of filing of the original certificate, the name under which the
-- corporation was originally incorporated, its name when the certificate became forfeited or void, and the new name
-- "to the extent required by subsection (f)"; (2) the registered office and agent; (3) that the corporation was organized
-- under the laws of this State; (4) the date the certificate became forfeited or void, "or that the validity of any revival
-- has been brought into question"; (5) that the certificate of revival is filed by authority of the board or governing body
-- in accordance with subsection (h).
-- src:1609 | (d) The certificate required by subsection (c) of this section shall state:
-- src:1610 | (1) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation; the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated; the name of the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title; and the new name under which the corporation is to be revived to the extent required by subsection (f) of this section;
-- src:1611 | (2) The address (which shall be stated in accordance with § 131(c) of this title) of the corporation’s registered office in this State and the name of its registered agent at such address;
-- src:1612 | (3) That the corporation desiring to be revived and so reviving its certificate of incorporation was organized under the laws of this State;
-- src:1613 | (4) The date when the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, or that the validity of any revival has been brought into question; and
-- src:1614 | (5) That the certificate of revival is filed by authority of the board of directors or members of the governing body of the corporation in accordance with subsection (h) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(d) (src:1609-1614)
DECLARE `s 312(d) Certificate of revival` HAS
    `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the name of the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the new name under which the corporation is to be revived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the address of the registered office in this State, stated in accordance with § 131(c), and the name of the registered agent at that address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that the corporation desiring to be revived was organized under the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date when the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, or that the validity of any revival has been brought into question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that the certificate is filed by authority of the board of directors or members of the governing body in accordance with subsection (h)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1609 | (d) The certificate required by subsection (c) of this section shall state:
-- src:1610 | (1) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation; the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated; the name of the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title; and the new name under which the corporation is to be revived to the extent required by subsection (f) of this section;
-- src:1611 | (2) The address (which shall be stated in accordance with § 131(c) of this title) of the corporation’s registered office in this State and the name of its registered agent at such address;
-- src:1612 | (3) That the corporation desiring to be revived and so reviving its certificate of incorporation was organized under the laws of this State;
-- src:1613 | (4) The date when the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, or that the validity of any revival has been brought into question; and
-- src:1614 | (5) That the certificate of revival is filed by authority of the board of directors or members of the governing body of the corporation in accordance with subsection (h) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(d) (src:1609-1614)
GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `s 312(d) Certificate of revival`
      `subsection (f) requires the corporation to be revived under a new name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(d) the certificate of revival states what the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the certificate`'s `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the name of the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void`
    AND ((NOT `subsection (f) requires the corporation to be revived under a new name`) OR `the certificate`'s `statement of the new name under which the corporation is to be revived`)
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the address of the registered office in this State, stated in accordance with § 131(c), and the name of the registered agent at that address`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement that the corporation desiring to be revived was organized under the laws of this State`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date when the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, or that the validity of any revival has been brought into question`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement that the certificate is filed by authority of the board of directors or members of the governing body in accordance with subsection (h)`

-- Subsection (e): "Upon the filing of the certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title the corporation shall be revived
-- with the same force and effect as if its certificate of incorporation had not been forfeited or void".
-- src:1615 | Upon the filing of the certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title the corporation shall be revived with the same force and effect as if its certificate of incorporation had not been forfeited or void pursuant to this title. Such revival shall validate all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done and performed within the scope of its certificate of incorporation by the corporation, its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and stockholders or members during the time when its certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void pursuant to this title, with the same force and effect and to all intents and purposes as if the certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full force and effect. All real and personal property, rights and credits, which belonged to the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title and which were not disposed of prior to the time of its revival, and all real and personal property, rights and credits acquired by the corporation after its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title shall be vested in the corporation, after its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full force and effect, and the corporation after its revival shall be as exclusively liable for all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done or performed in its name and on its behalf by its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and stockholders or members prior to its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full force and effect.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(e) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the certificate of revival was filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(e) the corporation is revived with the same force and effect as if its certificate had not been forfeited or void` MEANS
    `the certificate of revival was filed in accordance with § 103`

-- "Such revival shall validate all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done and performed within the scope of its
-- certificate of incorporation by the corporation, its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and
-- stockholders or members during the time when its certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void". Only those are
-- validated; for any other the text says nothing.
-- src:1615 | Such revival shall validate all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done and performed within the scope of its certificate of incorporation by the corporation, its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and stockholders or members during the time when its certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void pursuant to this title, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(e) (src:1615)
DECLARE `s 312(e) Person who made, did or performed the contract, act, matter or thing` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation itself`
    `a director or member of the governing body of the corporation`
    `an officer of the corporation`
    `an agent of the corporation`
    `a stockholder or member of the corporation`
    `someone else`

-- src:1615 | Such revival shall validate all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done and performed within the scope of its certificate of incorporation by the corporation, its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and stockholders or members during the time when its certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void pursuant to this title, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(e) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person` IS A `s 312(e) Person who made, did or performed the contract, act, matter or thing`
      `it was made, done or performed within the scope of the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made, done or performed during the time when the certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(e) the revival validates the contract, act, matter or thing` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)`
       AND (CONSIDER `the person`
            WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE)
       AND `it was made, done or performed within the scope of the certificate of incorporation`
       AND `it was made, done or performed during the time when the certificate of incorporation was forfeited or void`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "All real and personal property, rights and credits, which belonged to the corporation at the time its certificate of
-- incorporation became forfeited or void ... and which were not disposed of prior to the time of its revival, and all real and
-- personal property, rights and credits acquired by the corporation after its certificate of incorporation became forfeited
-- or void ... shall be vested in the corporation, after its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times
-- remained in full force and effect".
-- src:1615 | All real and personal property, rights and credits, which belonged to the corporation at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title and which were not disposed of prior to the time of its revival, and all real and personal property, rights and credits acquired by the corporation after its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title shall be vested in the corporation, after its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full force and effect, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(e) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property, right or credit belonged to the corporation when its certificate became forfeited or void and was not disposed of before the revival` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property, right or credit was acquired by the corporation after its certificate became forfeited or void` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(e) the property, right or credit is vested in the corporation after its revival` MEANS
        `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)`
    AND (    `the property, right or credit belonged to the corporation when its certificate became forfeited or void and was not disposed of before the revival`
         OR  `the property, right or credit was acquired by the corporation after its certificate became forfeited or void`)

-- "and the corporation after its revival shall be as exclusively liable for all contracts, acts, matters and things made,
-- done or performed in its name and on its behalf by its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and
-- stockholders or members prior to its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full
-- force and effect."
-- src:1615 | and the corporation after its revival shall be as exclusively liable for all contracts, acts, matters and things made, done or performed in its name and on its behalf by its directors or members of its governing body, officers, agents and stockholders or members prior to its revival, as if its certificate of incorporation had at all times remained in full force and effect.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(e) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person` IS A `s 312(e) Person who made, did or performed the contract, act, matter or thing`
      `it was made, done or performed in the name and on behalf of the corporation prior to its revival` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(e) the corporation is as exclusively liable for the contract, act, matter or thing as if its certificate had at all times remained in force` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation has been revived under section 312(e)`
       AND (CONSIDER `the person`
            WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `the corporation itself` THEN FALSE
