-- Subsection (f): if since the forfeiture another corporation of this State, or a foreign corporation qualified in accordance
-- with section 371 (out of range: piece dg10), has adopted the same name or one so nearly similar as not to distinguish it,
-- "the corporation to be revived shall not be revived under the same name ... but shall be revived under some other name".
-- src:1616 | (f) If, since the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, any other corporation organized under the laws of this State shall have adopted the same name as the corporation sought to be revived or shall have adopted a name so nearly similar thereto as not to distinguish it from the corporation to be revived or any foreign corporation qualified in accordance with § 371 of this title shall have adopted the same name as the corporation sought to be revived or shall have adopted a name so nearly similar thereto as not to distinguish it from the corporation to be revived, then in such case the corporation to be revived shall not be revived under the same name which it bore when its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title, but shall be revived under some other name as set forth in the certificate to be filed pursuant to subsection (c) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(f) (src:1616)
GIVEN `since the certificate became forfeited or void, another corporation organized under the laws of this State has adopted the same name as the corporation to be revived, or a name so nearly similar as not to distinguish it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `since the certificate became forfeited or void, a foreign corporation qualified in accordance with § 371 has adopted the same name as the corporation to be revived, or a name so nearly similar as not to distinguish it` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 371 (piece dg10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(f) the corporation to be revived must be revived under some other name` MEANS
        `since the certificate became forfeited or void, another corporation organized under the laws of this State has adopted the same name as the corporation to be revived, or a name so nearly similar as not to distinguish it`
    OR  `since the certificate became forfeited or void, a foreign corporation qualified in accordance with § 371 has adopted the same name as the corporation to be revived, or a name so nearly similar as not to distinguish it`

-- Subsection (g): the corporation pays "a sum equal to all franchise taxes, penalties and interest thereon due at the time its
-- certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void; provided, however, that any corporation that revives its certificate
-- of incorporation under this chapter whose certificate of incorporation has been forfeited or void for more than 5 years
-- shall, in lieu of the payment of the franchise taxes and penalties otherwise required by this subsection, pay a sum equal
-- to 3 times the amount of the annual franchise tax that would be due and payable by such corporation for the year in
-- which the revival is effected, computed at the then current rate of taxation." Reading taken (fork F14): "more than 5
-- years" is strictly more: the revival must fall after the 5th anniversary of the date the certificate became forfeited or void.
-- The franchise tax is chapter 5 of the Law (not among the inputs): the figures are plain inputs.
-- src:1617 | Any corporation that revives its certificate of incorporation under this chapter shall pay to this State a sum equal to all franchise taxes, penalties and interest thereon due at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title; provided, however, that any corporation that revives its certificate of incorporation under this chapter whose certificate of incorporation has been forfeited or void for more than 5 years shall, in lieu of the payment of the franchise taxes and penalties otherwise required by this subsection, pay a sum equal to 3 times the amount of the annual franchise tax that would be due and payable by such corporation for the year in which the revival is effected, computed at the then current rate of taxation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(g) (src:1617)
`s 312(g) the time after which a forfeited or void certificate costs 3 times the annual franchise tax to revive` MEANS `period in years` 5

-- src:1617 | Any corporation that revives its certificate of incorporation under this chapter shall pay to this State a sum equal to all franchise taxes, penalties and interest thereon due at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void pursuant to this title; provided, however, that any corporation that revives its certificate of incorporation under this chapter whose certificate of incorporation has been forfeited or void for more than 5 years shall, in lieu of the payment of the franchise taxes and penalties otherwise required by this subsection, pay a sum equal to 3 times the amount of the annual franchise tax that would be due and payable by such corporation for the year in which the revival is effected, computed at the then current rate of taxation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(g) (src:1617)
`s 312(g) the multiple of the annual franchise tax paid in lieu` MEANS 3

@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(g) (src:1617)
GIVEN `the franchise taxes, penalties and interest due at the time the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: chapter 5 of the Law is not among the inputs
      `the annual franchise tax that would be due and payable for the year in which the revival is effected, at the then current rate of taxation` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: chapter 5 of the Law is not among the inputs
      `the date the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void` IS A DATE
      `the date the revival is effected` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 312(g) the sum the corporation pays to this State on revival` MEANS
    IF `the date the revival is effected` GREATER THAN (`the date` `s 312(g) the time after which a forfeited or void certificate costs 3 times the annual franchise tax to revive` `after` `the date the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void`)
    THEN `s 312(g) the multiple of the annual franchise tax paid in lieu` TIMES `the annual franchise tax that would be due and payable for the year in which the revival is effected, at the then current rate of taxation`
    ELSE `the franchise taxes, penalties and interest due at the time the certificate of incorporation became forfeited or void`

-- "No payment made pursuant to this subsection shall reduce the amount of franchise tax due under Chapter 5 of this title
-- for the year in which the revival is effected."
-- src:1617 | No payment made pursuant to this subsection shall reduce the amount of franchise tax due under Chapter 5 of this title for the year in which the revival is effected. If the filing of a certificate of validation under § 204 of this title relates to a time during which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void, the annual reports and annual franchise taxes that would have been required to be filed and paid during the period in which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void, including interest thereon, are required to be filed and paid at the time of the filing of such certificate of validation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(g) (src:1617)
GIVEN `the franchise tax due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revival is effected` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: chapter 5 of the Law is not among the inputs
      `the payment made pursuant to subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 312(g) the franchise tax still due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revival is effected` MEANS
    `the franchise tax due under Chapter 5 for the year in which the revival is effected`

-- "If the filing of a certificate of validation under § 204 of this title relates to a time during which the corporation’s
-- certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void, the annual reports and annual franchise taxes that would have
-- been required to be filed and paid during the period in which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been
-- forfeited or void, including interest thereon, are required to be filed and paid at the time of the filing of such certificate
-- of validation." Section 204 is out of range (piece dg4).
-- src:1617 | If the filing of a certificate of validation under § 204 of this title relates to a time during which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void, the annual reports and annual franchise taxes that would have been required to be filed and paid during the period in which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void, including interest thereon, are required to be filed and paid at the time of the filing of such certificate of validation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(g) (src:1617)
GIVEN `a certificate of validation under § 204 is filed` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 204 (piece dg4)
      `the certificate of validation relates to a time during which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(g) the annual reports and franchise taxes for the period of forfeiture, with interest, must be filed and paid when the certificate of validation is filed` MEANS
    `a certificate of validation under § 204 is filed` AND `the certificate of validation relates to a time during which the corporation’s certificate of incorporation had been forfeited or void`

-- Subsection (h), first sentence: "the board of directors or governing body of the corporation shall be comprised of the persons,
-- who, but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly
-- elected or appointed directors or members of the governing body of the corporation."
-- src:1618 | For purposes of this section and § 502(a) of this title, the board of directors or governing body of the corporation shall be comprised of the persons, who, but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly elected or appointed directors or members of the governing body of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(h) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the person would be a duly elected or appointed director or member of the governing body but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(h) the person is a member of the board of directors or governing body for the purposes of section 312` MEANS
    `the person would be a duly elected or appointed director or member of the governing body but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title`

-- Second and third sentences: the authorization required by subsection (c) "shall be satisfied if a majority of the directors or
-- members of the governing body then in office, even though less than a quorum, or the sole director or member of the
-- governing body then in office, authorizes the revival ... and the filing of the certificate". Where no director is available
-- "the stockholders may elect a full board of directors, as provided by the bylaws of the corporation, and the board so
-- elected may then authorize the revival". The sole director is a majority of one, so one count covers both.
-- src:1618 | The requirement for authorization by the board of directors under subsection (c) of this section shall be satisfied if a majority of the directors or members of the governing body then in office, even though less than a quorum, or the sole director or member of the governing body then in office, authorizes the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation and the filing of the certificate required by subsection (c) of this section. …
-- src:1618 | In any case where there shall be no directors of the corporation available for the purposes aforesaid, the stockholders may elect a full board of directors, as provided by the bylaws of the corporation, and the board so elected may then authorize the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation and the filing of the certificate required by subsection (c) of this section. A special meeting of the stockholders for the purpose of electing directors may be called by any officer or stockholder upon notice given in accordance with § 222 of this title. For purposes of this section, the bylaws shall be the bylaws of the corporation that, but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(h) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the number of directors or members of the governing body then in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who authorize the revival and the filing of the certificate` IS A NUMBER
      `the stockholders elected a full board of directors as provided by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board so elected authorized the revival and the filing of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(h) the requirement for authorization by the board of directors is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors or members of the governing body then in office` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors then in office`) `the number of them who authorize the revival and the filing of the certificate` `the number of directors or members of the governing body then in office`
    ELSE JUST (`the stockholders elected a full board of directors as provided by the bylaws` AND `the board so elected authorized the revival and the filing of the certificate`)

-- "A special meeting of the stockholders for the purpose of electing directors may be called by any officer or stockholder
-- upon notice given in accordance with § 222 of this title." The caller is a party of the core's cast; any other party may not
-- call it under this sentence.
-- src:1618 | A special meeting of the stockholders for the purpose of electing directors may be called by any officer or stockholder upon notice given in accordance with § 222 of this title. For purposes of this section, the bylaws shall be the bylaws of the corporation that, but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(h) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the person calling the meeting` IS AN Actor
      `notice is given in accordance with § 222` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 222 (piece dg5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(h) the person may call a special meeting of the stockholders for the purpose of electing directors` MEANS
        (CONSIDER `the person calling the meeting`
         WHEN `an officer` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a stockholder` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `notice is given in accordance with § 222`

-- "For purposes of this section, the bylaws shall be the bylaws of the corporation that, but for the certificate of incorporation
-- having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation."
-- src:1618 | For purposes of this section, the bylaws shall be the bylaws of the corporation that, but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title, would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(h) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the instrument would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(h) the instrument is the bylaws of the corporation for the purposes of section 312` MEANS
    `the instrument would be the duly adopted bylaws of the corporation but for the certificate of incorporation having become forfeited or void pursuant to this title`

-- Subsection (i): after the revival "the provisions of § 211(c) of this title shall govern and the period of time during which
-- the certificate of incorporation of the corporation was forfeited or void pursuant to this title shall be included within the
-- calculation of the 30-day and 13-month periods to which § 211(c) of this title refers. A special meeting of stockholders
-- held in accordance with subsection (h) of this section shall be deemed an annual meeting of stockholders for purposes of
-- § 211(c) of this title." Subsection (j) takes subsection (i) out for a nonstock corporation. Section 211(c) is out of range
-- (piece dg4).
-- src:1619 | (i) After a revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation shall have been effected, the provisions of § 211(c) of this title shall govern and the period of time during which the certificate of incorporation of the corporation was forfeited or void pursuant to this title shall be included within the calculation of the 30-day and 13-month periods to which § 211(c) of this title refers. A special meeting of stockholders held in accordance with subsection (h) of this section shall be deemed an annual meeting of stockholders for purposes of § 211(c) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(i) (src:1619)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the revival of the certificate of incorporation has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(i) the period the certificate was forfeited or void is included within the calculation of the periods to which section 211(c) refers` MEANS
        `the revival of the certificate of incorporation has been effected`
    AND `s 312(j) subsection (i) of section 312 applies to the corporation` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `the kind of corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(i) (src:1619)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the revival of the certificate of incorporation has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special meeting of stockholders was held in accordance with subsection (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(i) the special meeting of stockholders is deemed an annual meeting of stockholders for the purposes of section 211(c)` MEANS
        `the revival of the certificate of incorporation has been effected`
    AND `the special meeting of stockholders was held in accordance with subsection (h)`
    AND `s 312(j) subsection (i) of section 312 applies to the corporation` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `the kind of corporation`

-- Subsection (j): "except as otherwise provided in § 313", for a nonstock corporation "the governing body shall perform all the
-- acts necessary for the revival ... which are performed by the board of directors in the case of a corporation having capital
-- stock, and the members of any nonstock corporation who are entitled to vote for the election of members of its governing
-- body shall perform all the acts necessary, if any, ... which are performed by the stockholders"; and "subsection (i) of this
-- section shall not apply to nonstock corporations".
-- src:1620 | (j) Except as otherwise provided in § 313 of this title, whenever it shall be desired to revive the certificate of incorporation of any nonstock corporation, the governing body shall perform all the acts necessary for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation which are performed by the board of directors in the case of a corporation having capital stock, and the members of any nonstock corporation who are entitled to vote for the election of members of its governing body shall perform all the acts necessary, if any, for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation which are performed by the stockholders in the case of a corporation having capital stock. Except as otherwise provided in § 313 of this title, in all other respects, the procedure for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of a nonstock corporation shall conform, as nearly as may be applicable, to the procedure prescribed in this section for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of a corporation having capital stock; provided, however, that subsection (i) of this section shall not apply to nonstock corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(j) (src:1620)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 312(j) subsection (i) of section 312 applies to the corporation` MEANS
    NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`)

-- src:1620 | (j) Except as otherwise provided in § 313 of this title, whenever it shall be desired to revive the certificate of incorporation of any nonstock corporation, the governing body shall perform all the acts necessary for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation which are performed by the board of directors in the case of a corporation having capital stock, and the members of any nonstock corporation who are entitled to vote for the election of members of its governing body shall perform all the acts necessary, if any, for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of the corporation which are performed by the stockholders in the case of a corporation having capital stock. Except as otherwise provided in § 313 of this title, in all other respects, the procedure for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of a nonstock corporation shall conform, as nearly as may be applicable, to the procedure prescribed in this section for the revival of the certificate of incorporation of a corporation having capital stock; provided, however, that subsection (i) of this section shall not apply to nonstock corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 312(j) (src:1620)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the party who performs the act for a corporation having capital stock` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A Actor
`s 312(j) the party who performs the act for the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the party who performs the act for a corporation having capital stock`
          WHEN `a director` THEN `another party named in the provision` "a member of the governing body"
          WHEN `a stockholder` THEN `a member of a nonstock corporation`
          OTHERWISE `the party who performs the act for a corporation having capital stock`)
    ELSE `the party who performs the act for a corporation having capital stock`

§§ `s 313 Revival of certificate of incorporation or charter of exempt corporations`

-- Subsection (a): an exempt corporation (section 501(b), chapter 5: not among the inputs) whose certificate "has become
-- forfeited, pursuant to § 136(b) of this title for failure to obtain a registered agent, or inoperative and void, by operation
-- of § 510 of this title for failure to file annual franchise tax reports required, and for failure to pay taxes or penalties
-- from which it would have been exempt if the reports had been filed, shall be deemed to have filed all the reports and be
-- relieved of all the taxes and penalties, upon satisfactory proof submitted to the Secretary of State of its right to be
-- classified as an exempt corporation pursuant to § 501(b) of this title, and upon filing with the Secretary of State a
-- certificate of revival in manner and form as required by § 312 of this title."
-- src:1624 | (a) Every exempt corporation whose certificate of incorporation or charter has become forfeited, pursuant to § 136(b) of this title for failure to obtain a registered agent, or inoperative and void, by operation of § 510 of this title for failure to file annual franchise tax reports required, and for failure to pay taxes or penalties from which it would have been exempt if the reports had been filed, shall be deemed to have filed all the reports and be relieved of all the taxes and penalties, upon satisfactory proof submitted to the Secretary of State of its right to be classified as an exempt corporation pursuant to § 501(b) of this title, and upon filing with the Secretary of State a certificate of revival in manner and form as required by § 312 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 313(a) (src:1624)
GIVEN `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 501(b) of chapter 5 is not among the inputs
      `the certificate has become forfeited pursuant to § 136(b) for failure to obtain a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 136(b) (piece dg2)
      `the certificate has become inoperative and void by operation of § 510 for failure to file the annual franchise tax reports required and to pay the taxes or penalties from which it would have been exempt if the reports had been filed` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 510 of chapter 5 is not among the inputs
      `satisfactory proof of its right to be classified as an exempt corporation has been submitted to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of revival has been filed with the Secretary of State in manner and form as required by § 312` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 313(a) the exempt corporation is deemed to have filed all the reports and is relieved of all the taxes and penalties` MEANS
        `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)`
    AND (    `the certificate has become forfeited pursuant to § 136(b) for failure to obtain a registered agent`
         OR  `the certificate has become inoperative and void by operation of § 510 for failure to file the annual franchise tax reports required and to pay the taxes or penalties from which it would have been exempt if the reports had been filed`)
    AND `satisfactory proof of its right to be classified as an exempt corporation has been submitted to the Secretary of State`
    AND `a certificate of revival has been filed with the Secretary of State in manner and form as required by § 312`

-- Subsection (b): "Upon the filing by the corporation of the proof of classification as required by subsection (a) of this section,
-- the filing of the certificate of revival and payment of the required filing fees, the corporation shall be revived with the
-- same force and effect as provided in § 312(e) of this title for other corporations."
-- src:1625 | (b) Upon the filing by the corporation of the proof of classification as required by subsection (a) of this section, the filing of the certificate of revival and payment of the required filing fees, the corporation shall be revived with the same force and effect as provided in § 312(e) of this title for other corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 313(b) (src:1625)
GIVEN `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has filed the proof of classification as required by subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has filed the certificate of revival` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required filing fees have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 313(b) the exempt corporation is revived with the same force and effect as provided in section 312(e)` MEANS
        `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)`
    AND `the corporation has filed the proof of classification as required by subsection (a)`
    AND `the corporation has filed the certificate of revival`
    AND `the required filing fees have been paid`

-- Subsection (c): "Nothing contained in this section relieves any exempt corporation from filing the annual report required by
-- § 502 of this title."
-- src:1626 | Nothing contained in this section relieves any exempt corporation from filing the annual report required by § 502 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 313(c) (src:1626)
GIVEN `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 313(c) the exempt corporation must still file the annual report required by section 502` MEANS
    `the corporation is an exempt corporation within the meaning of § 501(b)`

§§ `s 314 Status of corporation`

-- "Any corporation desiring to renew, extend and continue its corporate existence shall, upon complying with applicable
-- constitutional provisions of this State, continue as provided in its certificate effecting the foregoing as a corporation and
-- shall, in addition to the rights, privileges and immunities conferred by its charter, possess and enjoy all the benefits of this
-- chapter, which are applicable to the nature of its business, and shall be subject to the restrictions and liabilities by this
-- chapter imposed on such corporations."
-- src:1630 | Any corporation desiring to renew, extend and continue its corporate existence shall, upon complying with applicable constitutional provisions of this State, continue as provided in its certificate effecting the foregoing as a corporation and shall, in addition to the rights, privileges and immunities conferred by its charter, possess and enjoy all the benefits of this chapter, which are applicable to the nature of its business, and shall be subject to the restrictions and liabilities by this chapter imposed on such corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 314 (src:1630)
GIVEN `the corporation desires to renew, extend and continue its corporate existence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has complied with the applicable constitutional provisions of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 314 the corporation continues as provided in its certificate, possesses the benefits of this chapter and is subject to its restrictions and liabilities` MEANS
    `the corporation desires to renew, extend and continue its corporate existence` AND `the corporation has complied with the applicable constitutional provisions of this State`
